<hr class="nsw-m-y-lg">

<p>A close button is a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> element with the class <code>.nsw-icon-button</code>. We use the 'close' material icon as the X icon. This icon is wrapped in a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> with the attribute <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>, so screen readers don't read the X icon.</p>

<p>The button also includes a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> with the <code>.sr-only</code> class to tell screen readers what the button's purpose is.</p>

<h3>Guidance</h3>
<div class="nsw-grid nsw-m-top-sm">
  <div class="nsw-col nsw-col-sm-6 nsw-docs__guideline">
    <div class="nsw-docs__guideline--do"><span class="material-icons nsw-material-icons" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true">check_circle</span><span>Do</span></div>
    <ul class="nsw-m-top-sm">
      <li>wrap the close icon within a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> element using the <code>.nsw-icon-button</code> class</li>
      <li>mark the decorative X icon with <code>aria-hidden="true"</code></li>
      <li>provide a descriptive accessible name using visually hidden text</li>
      <li>connect the button to its dismissal action before showing it</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="nsw-col nsw-col-sm-6 nsw-docs__guideline">
    <div class="nsw-docs__guideline--dont"><span class="material-icons nsw-material-icons" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true">cancel</span><span>Don't</span></div>
    <ul class="nsw-m-top-sm">
      <li>use the X icon alone as the button's accessible name</li>
      <li>expose the decorative X icon to screen readers</li>
      <li>show a close button when it cannot perform its intended action</li>
      <li>use a close button for an action other than dismissing its associated interface element</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

